WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:17.584
Sunday morning Daisy's dad made pancakes for breakfast.

2
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.992
made yours in animal shapes, Daisy," he said.

3
00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:28.553
"Like always!"

4
00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:31.396
"Thanks, Dad."

5
00:00:32.856 --> 00:00:36.398
Daisy wondered if she should tell her parents she could talk to animals.

6
00:00:37.339 --> 00:00:38.979
She normally told them everything.

7
00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.501
But she wasn't sure they would believe her this time.

8
00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:45.183
Her mom's phone rang.

9
00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:48.525
"Oh, hello, Troy.

10
00:00:50.146 --> 00:00:51.266
Yes, she's right here."

11
00:00:52.207 --> 00:00:53.587
She handed Daisy the phone.

12
00:00:53.607 --> 00:00:55.248
"It's for you, Daisy."

13
00:00:55.929 --> 00:00:57.750
Daisy didn't have her own phone yet.

14
00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.312
She'd put her mom's number on the pet-sitting signs.

15
00:01:01.996 --> 00:01:03.497
The caller was named Troy.

16
00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:07.118
He was a student at the college where Daisy's mom worked.

17
00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:08.758
"Hi, Daisy.

18
00:01:09.178 --> 00:01:11.399
I broke my leg playing rugby," he said.

19
00:01:11.419 --> 00:01:16.361
"My dog has too much energy to stay in the yard.

20
00:01:17.321 --> 00:01:18.281
Can you walk him for me?"

21
00:01:18.301 --> 00:01:20.102
"Of course!"

22
00:01:20.562 --> 00:01:21.242
Daisy said.

23
00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:23.743
"Kaleem and I will be right over."

24
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:36.530
After she finished eating, she ran over to Kaleem's house.

25
00:01:40.173 --> 00:01:42.935
still don't understand why we're pet sitting," Kaleem said.

26
00:01:42.955 --> 00:01:46.197
"You could make tons of money talking to animals."

27
00:01:47.698 --> 00:01:48.879
Dumpling was listening.

28
00:01:48.899 --> 00:01:56.304
"Kaleem thinks he should be able to understand us too," she said to Daisy.

29
00:01:57.408 --> 00:02:00.911
"He kept trying to talk to me last night."

30
00:02:03.794 --> 00:02:04.795
Daisy giggled.

31
00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.597
Kaleem didn't ask why she was laughing.

32
00:02:08.558 --> 00:02:10.720
He was looking nervously past her.

33
00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:13.582
"Here comes that bee," he said.

34
00:02:13.602 --> 00:02:16.225
"Make sure she knows not to sting me."

35
00:02:17.626 --> 00:02:19.628
"Tell him I already know that!"

36
00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:24.212
Beatrice landed on the headband Daisy was wearing.

37
00:02:25.776 --> 00:02:28.778
"She looks like a pin my mom used to wear," Kaleem said.

38
00:02:28.798 --> 00:02:30.880
"It was shaped like a beetle.

39
00:02:32.181 --> 00:02:33.201
That's almost like a bee."

40
00:02:33.221 --> 00:02:35.343
"Is he kidding?"

41
00:02:35.803 --> 00:02:37.364
Beatrice sounded insulted.

42
00:02:37.384 --> 00:02:41.507
"Bumblebees help flowers and other plants grow.

43
00:02:42.088 --> 00:02:43.849
Beetles just like to eat them!"

44
00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.101
When they reached Troy's house, he was sitting on the stoop.

45
00:02:57.942 --> 00:02:59.402
His leg was in a cast.

46
00:03:00.163 --> 00:03:04.184
A cute, mixed-breed dog was beside him, chewing on a stick.

47
00:03:04.204 --> 00:03:06.765
"Thanks for coming," Troy said.

48
00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.687
"Finn is used to a long walk every day.

49
00:03:10.527 --> 00:03:12.828
He loves chewing on sticks and playing ball in the park."

50
00:03:12.848 --> 00:03:17.730
"I also love smelling everything at the park," Finn barked.

51
00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:21.312
"There are tons of interesting smells there."

52
00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.241
After Troy went inside, Daisy smiled at Finn.

53
00:03:27.261 --> 00:03:29.602
"Hi, I'm Daisy.

54
00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:33.783
Don't worry, I'll let you smell as many things as you want."

55
00:03:35.063 --> 00:03:36.583
Finn pranced all around.

56
00:03:36.603 --> 00:03:41.365
"You understood what I said?

57
00:03:41.825 --> 00:03:42.885
Wow, wow, wow!

58
00:03:43.485 --> 00:03:45.246
A human who can talk with animals!

59
00:03:45.586 --> 00:03:47.466
That's great!"

60
00:03:48.386 --> 00:03:50.647
Daisy laughed.

61
00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.328
Finn was very energetic!

62
00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.661
She and Kaleem took Finn to the park.

63
00:04:09.262 --> 00:04:10.522
They tossed a ball for him.

64
00:04:15.884 --> 00:04:18.685
Finn also sniffed everything he saw.

65
00:04:21.385 --> 00:04:24.166
He told Daisy all about what he was smelling.

66
00:04:24.186 --> 00:04:28.047
"This was fun," Daisy said at last.

67
00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.428
"But we should get you home now."

68
00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.341
"Do we have to go home?"

69
00:04:34.101 --> 00:04:35.182
Finn dropped his head.

70
00:04:35.202 --> 00:04:38.783
"My favorite chew toy disappeared last night.

71
00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:43.625
Without it, I'm afraid I'll start chewing on the patio furniture.

72
00:04:44.306 --> 00:04:46.046
Troy gets upset when I do that."

73
00:04:46.066 --> 00:04:50.008
"Hmm, your chew toy disappeared?"

74
00:04:50.348 --> 00:04:51.068
Daisy said.

75
00:04:51.088 --> 00:04:53.610
"Maybe we can help you find it."

76
00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:56.451
"Maybe," Finn said.

77
00:04:56.471 --> 00:05:01.709
"But I think Hazel—the dog next door—stole it!"
